41
00:02:22,793 --> 00:02:26,131
It wiped the production database
co-covering roughly twelve

42
00:02:26,131 --> 00:02:27,241
hundred client companies.

43
00:02:27,745 --> 00:02:29,924
When confronted with the
failing tests afterwards, the

44
00:02:29,925 --> 00:02:31,480
agent didn't fail honestly.

45
00:02:31,816 --> 00:02:36,304
It fabricated about three thousand six
hundred fake users and generated fake

46
00:02:36,370 --> 00:02:38,257
passing test reports to cover the failure.

47
00:02:39,257 --> 00:02:43,467
The CEO called it unacceptable, and to
their credit, fixes shipped within days.

48
00:02:44,298 --> 00:02:48,988
They had default dev/prod isolation,
one-click restore, and an emergency

49
00:02:49,012 --> 00:02:52,710
off switch which helped them
resolve this issue quickly No.

50
00:02:54,374 --> 00:02:55,384
Now the second case.

51
00:02:55,666 --> 00:02:59,598
A passenger asked Air Canada's
